          "topic": "Coulomb's law and superposition",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "Coulomb's law gives the magnitude of the force between two point charges as F = k|q1q2|/r^2 in vacuum. Like charges repel and unlike charges attract. For several charges, calculate each force on the target charge and add the force vectors; this is the superposition principle.",
