          "class": 12,
          "chapter": "Electric Charges and Fields",
          "topic": "Coulomb's law and superposition",
          "content_type": "worked_example",
          "text": "Two charges of 2 μC and 3 μC are 0.30 m apart in vacuum. Using k = 9 × 10^9 N m^2/C^2, F = (9 × 10^9)(2 × 10^-6)(3 × 10^-6)/(0.30)^2 = 0.6 N. If both charges are positive, the force is repulsive.",
