          "topic": "Capacitors in series and parallel",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "For capacitors in parallel, each has the same potential difference and equivalent capacitance is the sum. In series, each carries equal-magnitude charge and reciprocal capacitances add. These rules follow from the circuit connections.",
