          "topic": "Faraday’s law and Lenz’s law",
          "content_type": "explanation",
          "text": "An emf is induced when magnetic flux through a circuit changes. Faraday’s law gives ε = −dΦB/dt for one loop; the negative sign expresses Lenz’s law: induced effects oppose the change in flux that produced them.",
